      "section": "Electrical Shock Hazard",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 126.6942,
        "t": 615.3082318,
        "r": 237.46759379999995,
        "b": 606.6307174112267
      },
      "content": "Electrical Shock Hazard",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0578",
      "reading_order": 650,
      "section": "Electrical Shock Hazard",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 65.30866169999999,
        "t": 600.1645768000001,
        "r": 272.68880429999996,
        "b": 581.2284574112267
      },
      "content": "Only authorized technicians should perform diagnostic voltage measurements."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0579",
      "reading_order": 651,
      "section": "Electrical Shock Hazard",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 65.30866169999999,
        "t": 574.7623168000001,
        "r": 256.4118177,
        "b": 555.8261974112268
      },
      "content": "After performing voltage measurements, disconnect power before servicing."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0580",
      "reading_order": 652,
      "section": "Electrical Shock Hazard",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 65.30866169999999,
        "t": 549.3600568000002,
        "r": 290.0795823,
        "b": 530.4239374112268
      },
      "content": "Failure to follow these instructions can result in death or electrical shock."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0581",
      "reading_order": 653,
      "section": "Turbidity Sensor",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 54.5625,
        "t": 502.112,
        "r": 162.62650000000002,
        "b": 489.9393613445378
      },
      "content": "Turbidity Sensor",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0582",
      "reading_order": 654,
      "section": "Overview",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 54.5625,
        "t": 468.584,
        "r": 102.2025,
        "b": 459.4545210084034
      },
      "content": "Overview",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0583",
      "reading_order": 655,
      "section": "Overview",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 54.5625,
        "t": 454.32,
        "r": 308.31249999999994,
        "b": 416.7121008403361
      },
      "content": "The turbidity sensor is located under the tub and is attached to the sump with two snap clips (see Figure 1). During the prewash cycle, the turbidity sensor senses the water and chooses the appropriate wash cycle."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0584",
      "reading_order": 656,
      "section": "Overview",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 54.5625,
        "t": 411.32,
        "r": 311.8125,
        "b": 393.7121008403361
      },
      "content": "NOTE : If the turbidity sensor is not functioning, the dishwasher will continue to operate, but choose a default wash cycle."
    },
    {
